# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this the build context is the whole
# working tree — .git alone is 230MB+. That is uploaded to the remote builder on
# every deploy before any layer can be cached, which is most of the deploy's wall
# clock and none of its value: the build needs the Go sources and go.mod, nothing else.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Local build output. The binary is rebuilt inside the image; shipping the host's
# copy in is both useless and a 33MB tax — and a stale one, since it is whatever
# was last compiled locally.
/opentrace
*.exe
dist/
bin/

# Runtime and scratch data, including local log segments and SQLite files.
tmp/
data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log

# Docs, deployment configs for other platforms, and editor state: none of it is
# compiled and all of it invalidates the context on every edit.
docs/
deploy/
*.md
!README.md
railway.toml
render.yaml
fly.toml
docker-compose*.yml
.env
.env.*
.mcp.json
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Tests do not run in the image build.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/
